  "notes": "RSS feeds expose only their latest items and cannot be re-fetched historically, so this is an append-only snapshot: the HF copy under news/rss/ is the archive of record and must be backed up and snapshotted at code freeze. Coverage before the first run (2026-11-08) is only what each feed still showed then. row_count = articles in the archive; file_count = article parquet partitions; files = this run's outputs. Dedupe is by canonical URL (slug dropped where configured); the first sighting of an article is kept and later edits are not captured, except in the raw feed snapshots. full_text is plain text from content:encoded when the feed includes it. Business Recorder's RSS shows only 30 items and publishes in bursts, so its news sitemap (100 latest) is also read each run and missing articles are fetched from their pages (feed_role='sitemap', full_text_source='article_page'). language is the feed-declared code, or 'ur' when the title is mostly Arabic script. tickers_mentioned is empty until tagging is built.",
